e of calamity was  it unfortunately left us with two  different versions of events which are  incompatible with one another  on one side we have breath of the wild  plus creating a champion  and on the other we have age of calamity  so what are the biggest differences when  it comes to how link got the sword in  these two different timelines  well to start off creating a champion  established that link got the legendary  blade  years before the events of the calamity  and the book makes this clear  on multiple occasions first off we have  the part which has been referenced  numerous times by other theorists which  is this section on page 376  where it states that he was in  possession of the sword for a number of  years prior to becoming a champion and  he was likely around  12 or 13 years old when it happened and  second the event of link extracting the  master sword is listed as something that  occurred  even before the sheikah slate was even  discovered and as we all know at the  beginning of age of calamity  impa is already in possession of the  slate days before link travels to korok  forest to pull the master sword  link is also already 17 years old in  this story when he acquires the sword  whereas in the book he was supposedly 12  or 13. now you might say well  age of calamity involves time travel  right so the timing of events simply  changed because of that  well no that would be impossible the  game makes it clear that age of  calamity's reality did not exist until  terrico jumped into the past  so assuming that age of calamity is a  traditional timeline split like the one  from ocarina of time  anything that happened before terraco  arrived in the past would have to be a  carbon copy of breath the wild storyline  since it quite literally splits off of  that timeline and it is only then that  things start changing because of his  influence  tereko arrives only a few weeks before  the calamity is set to occur  the champions have not been approached  yet but the sheikah slate has already  been discovered making it impossible for  his presence to have had  any effect on how and when link got the  sword he should have already been in  possession of the sword when the  guardian arrives but as we all know  that's not the case  so right away this leaves us with two  completely different chronologies  and under normal circumstances we would  simply have to make the consideration of  which piece of media holds more weight  in terms of canonicity  a third-party book or a third-party game  i've spoken to other theorists about  this at the time  and we agreed that a game would probably  have priority over a book if it was just  creating a champion versus age of  calamity in this case  however in my opinion there is one thing  that trumps both sources  altogether and that is breath of the  wild itself  hence in this particular case breath of  the wild would have to be the  determining factor  so which version of events does breath  of the wild side with  well at first it doesn't seem like the  game has much to say about how link got  the master sword  in every memory from 100 years ago he  already has it but it never makes it  clear when  and how that is until you get the second  dlc pack the champion's ballad here the  game sheds a bit more light on some of  the events which took place prior to the  calamity we see how zelda first  approached the pilots the ceremony where  they were officially appointed as  champions  some of the time they spent together as  a group etc but more importantly for  this topic is that we gain  access to the diaries of the four  champions personal memoirs in which they  describe their thoughts and experiences  both during and prior to the calamity  and on two occasions these stories  confirmed that not only did link  already have the master sword he was  also already selected as the chosen  knight who would slay ganon  long before the royal family even  started selecting candidates to pilot  the divine beasts  ravali describes his joy and pride when  zelda came to ask him to pilot vametto  only to quickly shift his tone as soon  as he found out that his role was  nothing more than that of a support for  some chosen knight he's never met before  and that he is not the one  tasked with taking gannon down himself  in turn mifa states that link came to  visit her at zora's domain right after  divine beast farouta was discovered but  before  zelda came to ask her to pilot the beast  and she specifically says that during  this visit  link already had the sword and mind you  even more time passes after that as it  took a while for her father king dorafan  to finally agree to mifa becoming the  champion of varuta  as at first he was hesitant for a while  link allegedly even fought a lino atop  pleime's mountain with the master sword  before her father gave his blessing  according to mifa's written word so by  the looks of it breath of the wild  points to creating a champion's version  of events being the true story  link already had the sword long before  the pilots were selected  age of calamity says no to that and here  link pulls the sword after the champions  obliged to pilot the beast  and in their presence no less and i  think we all know why this part of age  of calamity story is different they  simply didn't want link to start off  with the master sword  right at the beginning of the game and  from a gameplay perspective i get that  not only would it make a lot of the  early weapons useless i mean why would i  use a broadsword if i have the most  iconic and one of the more powerful  weapons in the game  and i'm pretty sure they also wanted to  have an epic master sword pull in this  story  it's kind of zelda tradition at this  point the first hyrule warriors had it  too  but the unfortunate side effect of this  change is that this part of the lord  does mess with that which breath of the  wild and the book has set up  all this could have been fixed by either  