s father before  him for the same reason that a  blacksmith's son would also become a  blacksmith when they grow up  we learned from mifa's diary that link  was exceptionally skilled in combat from  a very early age  being able to even best adults when he  was only around  4 years old a bit hard to believe but i  guess he is the chosen hero after all  i mean the hero of time defeated  monsters 10 times his size when he was  only 9 years old so  you know anyway if we were to go off of  what creating a champion tells us link  would have been around 12 to 13 years  old when he first pulled the master  sword which  is quite young but since link was  already quite powerful  even from a very young age this does  make sense the only reason why he wasn't  able to pull the sword in breath of the  wild initially is because of the stasis  he was put under for 100 years which  understandably took a massive toll on  him although it's never stated where  link found it i do think the master  sword was in the pedestal at korok  forest when he did  creating a champion states that the  master sword has averted many calamities  alongside past heroes  and that it's placed inside the pedestal  to recover from the damage it incurs  from those battles  as such since the last calamity was  successfully halted 10 000 years ago  it's only natural that back then they  followed the tradition of returning the  sword where it belongs  each time it fulfilled its role this  happens many times in other installments  as well where either the hero himself or  someone else returns the sword at the  end of the game  except in the wind waker i just got  stabbed in the face  now let's quickly talk about link's  origins where did he  initially come from despite no  definitive proof i'm quite sure that  link did indeed originate from hiteno  village  there are simply more hints that this  was the place where he was raised than  any other place in hyrule like the house  which was conveniently abandoned for 