ill a long  ways away for a boy his  age to be traveling here alone right  well there is one location which could  explain  everything one hylian structure close to  hyrule's great forest which could have  played a big role in this  since link was extremely talented with a  sword from a very young age  it probably didn't take long for his  father to draft him into hyrule's army  by the time link would join the army the  prophecy of ganon's return had already  come to light years prior  zelda was only 7 at the time and there's  only 1 year age gap between her and link  the hylian army likely needed every bit  of manpower they could get in  preparation for ganon's return so it's  only natural that an exceptionally  talented swordsman like link would be  more than welcome despite his young  age and where does anyone go before they  join the actual army  exactly boot camp in this case hyrule's  military training camp close to the  border of hyrule's great forest  as is the case with many military  training camps the cadets often sleep in  barracks in and around the same area  so link likely spent at least a couple  of months at the training camp together  with the other recruits and it is during  this time that i believe link found his  way to the master sword  as is often the case with the master  sword the hero doesn't choose  it but rather the sword chooses the hero  and since ganon's return was only a few  years away  the sword was likely ready to be found  by the next hero worthy of wielding it  while present at the training camp  link may have felt a pull towards the  great forest  an unknown force calling out to him  until one night the young swordsman  finally gave into the temptation  sneaking away from the barracks to  venture into the misty forest alone  driven by intuition or perhaps guided by  some divine influence  he managed to make his way through the  forest successfully without getting lost  once he arrives at the foot of the great  deku tree he lay his eyes upon the  sparkling blade  and with that link pulls the master  sword perhaps without realizing that he  has been chosen for a great but  dangerous task which will determine the  future of hyrule  word quickly spread about the young man  who emerged carrying the legendary sword  that seals the darkness  and it wouldn't be long until he was  recognized as the one who would have to  face ganon alongside the princess faced  with a tremendous responsibility this is  also the time when links started to grow  more and more silent  going from a bold outspoken kid to a  silent and burdened young adult  and that is how i envisioned it  happening but that's just my take  on it perhaps you have a completely  different scenario in mind  i know i've been kinda harsh on age of  calamity in this video  but please bear in mind that i don't  dislike the game in any way  in the end it doesn't even really matter  as arlo stated in his review  of the game breath of the wild and age  of calamity are vastly different games  each with their own rules and mechanics  in one link struggles with a single  lynel even in the late game  and in the other he mows down enemies by  the thousands but that's the nature of a  warriors game  age of calamity was epic and although i  don't consider it as  canon as breath of the wild i still  think the master sword pull in that game  was very cool and unique  it happens under extreme pressure and  during a boss fight nonetheless  does it fit with breath the world's  narrative in my opinion  no but at the end of the day  entertainment is more important than  lore consistency  it would have been cool if we got both  but that's the curse of a spin-off game  i guess  thank you for watching let me know what  you think how do  you envision link got the master sword  in breath of the wild do you still fully  accept age of calamity as canon be sure  to leave a comment down below  a special shout out as always goes to my  amazing patreons and members who  co